---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals work with existing enterprise systems?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Enterprise projects often involve existing platforms, databases, APIs and operational processes. Integration or phased modernisation may be more appropriate than replacing everything.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can enterprise transformation be delivered in phases?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Phased delivery is usually preferable because dependencies, users and operational risks can be controlled more carefully than in a single large cutover.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can new systems integrate with existing ERP, CRM or third-party platforms?",
    answer:
      "Yes, where suitable integration mechanisms are available. APIs, data exchange and system boundaries should be reviewed early in the architecture process.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "How do you approach data migration?",
    answer:
      "Migration should include source assessment, mapping, validation, test migrations, ownership decisions and fallback planning rather than treating data transfer as a final deployment step.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do enterprise systems require ongoing maintenance?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Production systems, infrastructure, integrations, dependencies and security requirements continue to change after launch.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals support architecture and planning before development begins?",
    answer:
      "Yes. IT consultancy can be used before implementation to assess requirements, dependencies, integration constraints, risks and delivery options.",
  },
];
---

<section class="enterprise-faq">
  <div class="site-container enterprise-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Enterprise FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions worth resolving before large systems start moving.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="enterprise-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .enterprise-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .enterprise-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(17rem, 0.7fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .enterprise-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .enterprise-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .enterprise-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .enterprise-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .enterprise-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .enterprise-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .enterprise-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
